-- Rock compressibility by PVT region in a compositional run.  A row of 30 cells
-- holds oil of three components (CO2, methane, decane) and water, with the same
-- water in both PVT regions.  The ROCK record of region 1 (cells 1-15) has no
-- compressibility, and that of region 2 (cells 16-30) a compressibility of
-- 5E-4 /bar; both take 150 bar as the reference pressure.  There are no wells:
-- region 1 starts at 170 bar and region 2 at 130 bar, so the pressure evens out.
-- The compressibility, several times that of typical rock, makes its effect
-- on the pressure clear.
--
-- The pore volume of each cell follows the rock compressibility of its region.
-- As region 2 fills, its pores expand and take up more of the fluid, so the
-- pressure evens out at about 138.5 bar rather than the 149.4 bar that rock
-- without compressibility would give.
-- BRPV reports the pore volume directly: the cells of region 1 keep 1 m3,
-- while those of region 2 have 1 * (1 + x + x*x/2) m3, with
-- x = 5E-4 * (pressure in bar - 150).

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   COMPOSITIONAL TWO ROCK COMPRESSIBILITY REGIONS

METRIC

TABDIMS
1* 2 /
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
30 1 1
/

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/ROW_GRID.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/PROPS.inc' /

-- One record per PVT region.
ROCK
    150.0  0.0 /
    150.0  5.0E-4 /

PVTW
    75.0  1.03  4.0E-5  0.3  0.0 /
    75.0  1.03  4.0E-5  0.3  0.0 /

DENSITY
    800.0  1000.0  1.0 /
    800.0  1000.0  1.0 /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
PVTNUM
15*1 15*2
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/ROW_SOLUTION.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/ROW_SUMMARY.inc' /

-- Pore volumes at either end and on either side of the region boundary.
BRPV
1 1 1 /
15 1 1 /
16 1 1 /
30 1 1 /
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHEDULE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/REPORTING.inc' /

TSTEP
0.1 0.4 0.5 1.0 1.0 2.0
10*2.5
/
END
